notes:
/* The button becomes its own dialog. Nothing opens over the
   page, nothing shifts around it, and the choice stays under
   the cursor that asked for it — a modal moves your attention
   somewhere else to answer a question you just asked here.

   Undo lives in the same footprint too, on a timer, so the
   destructive path never needs a toast either. */

/* ONE PRESS. No confirmation step: it deletes at once and the
   same pill springs wide to say so and offer Undo — an undo
   that is right there asks only of the people who changed
   their mind. */
idle: [112]  "Delete"
done: [206]  "Deleted · Undo"   out with a little give, back firmly

/* how long undo is still on offer */
@keyframes burn { from { width: 100%; } to { width: 0; } }
